the retained calendar body hash exactly. Its artifact manifest records the bounded public-domain 1862 Pustet antecedent, the separate 1962 target, and every editorial transformation; neither witness is represented as owning the projected bytes. The 1962 reading was established on that edition's page images rather than its text layer, cross-read against the Benziger conformed printing. Differences from the antecedent: the Tours Mame 1922 window carries 'S' at this point where the 1962 does not; the Tours Mame 1922 reads 'xtérnz' where the 1962 prints 'aeternae:'; the Tours Mame 1922 reads 'futire.' where the 1962 prints 'futurae.'; recogniser damage in the Tours Mame 1922 text layer at this locus, not variant readings: Apostolis. for apostolo; UMPTUM, for sumptum; redemptidnis for redemptionis; quésumus; for quaesumus; Bartholomzo for bartholomaeo; Apdstolo for apostolo; vite for uitae; preséntis for praesentis; bare numeric tokens (printed folio / marginal numbers) dropped from the Tours Mame 1922 reading: 19, 28. 700; conclusion length was not collated: the 1962 prints 'Per Dominum.' and the witness abbreviates the same rubrical cue; one formula at two lengths, which is within the matched tolerance. Corroboration: Pustet Ratisbon 1862, nearest preceding printed-folio marker 516 at text-layer line 71280; text-layer lines 71370-71390 (char-level agreement 0.778 with the 1962 target).","relationship":"editorial-projection-exact-to-target","source_date":"2026-09-03 project editorial projection; antecedent Pustet Ratisbon 1862","source_id":"passage.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.s-bartholomaei-apostoli-postcommunion","status":"collated","transformations":["join printed line wraps","remove stress accents","expand printed ae/oe ligatures to ae/oe","normalise consonantal i to the calendar's j orthography","apply the target printing's punctuation","carry the target's conclusion at its printed length"],"verification_locator":"printed p. 636, no. 3453; artifact PDF p. 717","verification_source_id":"passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.temporal-s-bartholomaei-apostoli-orations"},"publication":{"basis":"public-domain","evidence":"The wording is preexisting material of the 1962 typical edition under 17 U.S.C. 103(b), which gives a revised edition no exclusive right in material it did not contribute. The independent registered public-domain witness is the tracked 1862 Pustet text artifact. The position is settled for the repository at src/sources/inventories/missale-romanum-1962-facsimile-rights-v1.toml, which names the seasonal orations as preexisting material and requires exactly this pairing of 103(b) with a public-domain witness.","locator":"Pustet Ratisbon 1862, Tours Mame 1922 (editio quarta iuxta typicam Vaticanam), printed p. 699; artifact PDF p. 813; column-correct raw-text lines 62420-62437; artifact rights_status public-domain","source_ids":["artifact.triptych.roman-1962-latin-proper-editorial-projection.editorial-projection-2026-09-03.gap-sanctoral-3-orations-b43e63f0","artifact.catholic-church.missale-romanum.pustet-ratisbon-1862.missale-romanum-1862-text-f34bc7cf"],"status":"permitted","surfaces":["cli","corpus-data","download","print","public-git","web"]},"reason":null,"text_sha256":"c8d2b6b7ed383e5e1e90a79f4f0c32f3923aba9b9f6f0944b4de936a467ba6fe","withheld":false},"name":"Postcommunion","source":"composed","taken_from":null,"text":"Sumptum, Domine, pignus redemptionis aeternae: sit nobis, quaesumus;\ninterveniente beato Bartholomaeo Apostolo tuo, vitae praesentis auxilium\npariter et futurae. Per Dominum.\n","text_status":null,"translations":[{"caution":"A lay hand missal of the 1945 revision, printed about 1955-56, not an approved liturgical translation and never an altar book. Its Holy Week is the pre-1955 rite, its sanctoral is not the 1962 sanctoral, and its second and third orations are not those of 1962. It is carried only where a 1962 formulary is the same prayer, and nothing here may be used for recitation.\n\nHistorical source s-bartholomaei-apostoli/main/Postcommunion/all/1; strict. Complete Latin word sequence and actual ending equal under typography only. Cross-owner reuse requires entire literal canonical Latin equality including conclusion, punctuation, wraps and final LF, SHA256 c8d2b6b7ed383e5e1e90a79f4f0c32f3923aba9b9f6f0944b4de936a467ba6fe. Original target proof passage.catholic-church.missale-romanum.vatican-typica-1962.temporal-s-bartholomaei-apostoli-orations retained. No source-recipient calendar attestation or official 1962 English claimed.","lang":"en","rights":"public-domain","source_id":"edition.francis-xavier-lasance.the-new-roman-missal.benziger-revised-1945","source_label":"The New Roman Missal in Latin and English, revised edition, by F. X. Lasance and Francis Augustine Walsh (New York: Benziger Brothers, 1945), ca. 1955-56 printing (Internet Archive delivery locator fr-lasance-missal-1937; locator mislabelled)","text":"May the pledge of everlasting redemption, which we have received, O Lord, be unto us, we beseech Thee, by the intercession of blessed Bartholomew Thine apostle, an aid alike for the present and the future life. Through our Lord."}],"unavailable_translations":null,"untranslated":null},{"appointment_identity":{"form_id":"main","mass":"s-bartholomaei-apostoli","occurrence":2,"proper":"Introit"},"citations":[{"book":"Psalms","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":64,"first":3,"last":3}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":64,"first":2,"last":2}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":63,"first":3,"last":3}]},"numbering":"vulgate","ref":"Psalms 63:3","token":"Ps","unresolved":null},{"book":"Psalms","loci":{"hebrew":[{"chapter":64,"first":2,"last":2}],"hebrew-unnumbered-titles":[{"chapter":64,"first":1,"last":1}],"vulgate":[{"chapter":63,"first":2,"last":2}]},"numbering":"vulgate","ref":"Psalms 63:2","token":"Ps","unresolved":null}],"coverage":{"component":"scripture","cycle":"all","cycle_fam